Original commit body from e4b845843f52bd90018a96b9de14e65cf4861a99:

bash is dataflow_capable=false, so every redirect-sink taint finding in a
shell script rested on call-graph reachability alone: "this file reads the
environment somewhere AND reaches a function that writes somewhere". A
two-file repro shows the failure directly -- `curl -L "$URL" > "$DEST"` and
`echo "version is $MSG" > banner.txt` produce findings that are byte-identical
in shape: same env.environ source at FILE granularity, same redirect.> sink,
same structural/unavailable walk.

The analyzer now closes name derivation over the whole file (assignments, for
bindings, and positional parameters bound at every call site of the enclosing
function) and stamps `redirect_origin_names`: the externally-derived names
that can reach what the SHELL ITSELF contributes -- the target operand, a
heredoc body it expands, and every producing stage's arguments. An EMPTY stamp
is a proof and joins _sink_call_can_carry_taint as its third arm; an ABSENT
stamp is not, and keeps the finding.

NOT the byte-producer question, which was measured wrong. "Is the writer
external?" deletes beads' `echo "$SIGNING_CERT" | base64 -d > cert.pfx`, where
a real certificate is written and only stage one is a builtin, and misreads
cilium's `sed -E "s#x#${v}#" f > out`, where an in-process value is
interpolated through an external command. The fetch case is deliberately left
open: `curl "$URL" > "$DEST"` still credits URL, because deciding curl's
argument merely SELECTS is per-command semantics this gate does not have.
Ablation prices that omission at 3 of 186 names and zero of 69 files.

A parse failure is not a proof of emptiness, and the scope that holds is the
file: cilium's `<<EOF cat >/etc/dnsmasq.conf` lands tree-sitter's ERROR node
on a SIBLING statement while the redirect parses cleanly, so a parent-scoped
guard read it as "no name reaches" over a body writing $ddns to a config file.
11 of 212 cohort bash files carrying a redirect contain an ERROR or MISSING
node (5.2%), so the conservative scope costs almost nothing.

Measured on 15 cohort repositories, both arms cold (15/15): 16 rows removed,
0 added, and NO claim verdict changed category -- every moved claim stays
violated with a lower count, so no all-clear was manufactured. All 16 removed
rows were read back against source across 14 files; every one writes literals
or locally-derived values, and every genuine carrier survives ($GITHUB_OUTPUT,
LICENSE_INFO_DIR, LINK_TO_ARTIFACT, a for-loop variable).

Refs WI-zovuz. INV-fumod shape (b) stays violated.

